<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Barbados Labour Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1938">1938</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Barbados Labour Party is one of the two main political parties of Barbados, founded in 1938 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grantley-adams">Grantley Adams</a> and others after the labour riots of 1937. It led the island towards universal suffrage and self-government, and later governed under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tom-adams">Tom Adams</a>, Owen Arthur and, from 2018, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mia-mottley">Mia Mottley</a>. It has alternated in power with the Democratic Labour Party, which broke away from it in 1955.</p></div>
